{
 "_doc": "Wawa locations in/near the market-history target towns, geocoded. Feeds nearest_wawa_mi in share/wawa_by_town.csv via build_share.py. Store list supplied 2026-07-16; coordinates resolved the same day.",
 "_intent": "Proximity to a Wawa is a NICE-TO-HAVE for a house, never a requirement. Reported as a soft signal (distance to the nearest store); MUST NOT filter, exclude, or rank out a town or a listing. No thresholds. Same contract as layers/seabra/ and layers/trader_joes/.",
 "_rejected_field": "The supplied JSON carried a `near_target_towns` array on every store plus a claim of 41 matched towns, from an approximate ~5mi locator match. IT IS NOT STORED HERE AND WAS NOT USED. Checked against real geocodes, 26 of its pairs break its own 5mi rule (it called Elizabeth 'near' Springfield at 7.2mi, and Linden-East 'near' Woodbridge at 6.9mi). Distance is computed from coordinates by build_share.py, exactly as for the other two amenity layers. A pre-baked town match is an answer, not data \u2014 never trust one you can compute.",
 "_coverage_caveat": "THE SHARPEST LIMIT ON THIS LAYER. The supplied list was itself filtered to stores 'in or near' the target set using a ~5mi cutoff, so it is NOT all NJ Wawas. It is therefore INCOMPLETE BY CONSTRUCTION for any town whose real nearest Wawa sits outside that cutoff: 9 of 53 towns compute to >5mi (Long Valley 13.1, Glen Rock 9.2, Chester 9.0, Franklin Lakes 9.0, Bedminster 8.5, ...) and for those the true nearest store may simply not be in this file. Read a large nearest_wawa_mi as 'no Wawa in the supplied set is close', NOT as 'there is no Wawa nearby'. The other 44 towns are within 5mi and are unaffected.",
 "_geocode_note": "26 of 31 rooftop via the US Census geocoder (key-less, cloud-safe). Census cannot resolve route-style addresses ('16 Route 46'), so 5 fell back to OpenStreetMap Nominatim: 3 by address (osm_nominatim) and 2 by brand+town POI (osm_poi, the coarsest \u2014 Pine Brook and Mountain Lakes). Precision rides on every row; treat osm_poi points as approximate.",
 "_schema": "locations[]: brand, name, store_number, town, county, state, zip, address, status, official_url, lat, lon, geocode_precision. `town`/`county`/`zip` are the STORE's own location \u2014 mostly NOT target towns. Do not join on them; this is a distance join.",
 "_caveats": [
  "Straight-line miles from a town's zip centroid to the store, NOT drive time (~1.3-1.5x in this area). Never quote it as a commute.",
  "Measured TOWN-to-store, so identical for every house in a town. A house's own address does not move it.",
  "Like Trader Joe's and unlike Seabra, some stores sit INSIDE target towns (Cranford, Springfield, Maplewood, Woodbridge, Edison x3, Bridgewater, Randolph). A ~0-1mi reading there is expected, not a bug.",
  "All 31 are status 'open'; the open_only filter in build_share.py is a no-op today but stays for when it isn't.",
  "official_url is retained per store for re-verification."
 ],
